expr main (in spite of the fact that)

let message "`in spite of the fact that` is wordy. Use `although`."
let description "Shortens `in spite of the fact that`."
let kind "Style"
let becomes "although"
let strategy "MatchCase"

test "In spite of the fact that, we left." "Although, we left."
test "We stayed in spite of the fact that, it rained." "We stayed although, it rained."
test "In spite of the fact that it was late, he called." "Although it was late, he called."
test "I came in spite of the fact that I was tired." "I came although I was tired."
test "She won in spite of the fact that the odds were against her." "She won although the odds were against her."
test "In spite of the fact that they argued, they stayed." "Although they argued, they stayed."
test "He smiled in spite of the fact that he was sad." "He smiled although he was sad."
test "We went out in spite of the fact that it snowed." "We went out although it snowed."
test "In spite of the fact that the delay, we won." "Although the delay, we won."
test "They finished in spite of the fact that it was hard." "They finished although it was hard."
test "In spite of the fact that the rain, we played." "Although the rain, we played."
test "I stayed in spite of the fact that it hurt." "I stayed although it hurt."

allows "Although, we left."
allows "We stayed although, it rained."
allows "Although it was late, he called."
allows "I came although I was tired."
allows "She won although the odds were against her."
allows "The weather is nice today."
allows "Please send the report by Friday."
allows "She enjoys long walks."
